As part of a (perhaps short-lived) fitness kick, Adrian is tracking his daily energy intake and starts by looking at a typical breakfast. He worked out the energy from his Weet-bix by reading the box but couldn't do the same with his milk.

Use the website calorieking.com/au/en/ to help complete the table below (Note: type in the food items exactly as they are presented below).

Consider the following average energies for these nutrients:

\begin{itemize}
\item Protein 17kJ/g
\item Fat 38kJ/g
\item Carbohydrate 17kJ/g
\item Dietary Fibre 8kJ/g
\end{itemize}

\extable{3307_q8_t1}

If Adrian calculated his BMR to be 7000kJ/day, and used the PAL values and formula shown below, how much energy would he expend if he decided to run at 9km/h for half an hour?

$$\text{Energy Out} = (\text{duration of activity in hours}) \times \left(\text{BMR in } \dfrac{\text{kJ}}{\text{hour}}\right) \times \text{PAL}$$

\extable{3307_q9_t1}
